-- THE BUILDING
--
-- Five rooms and the walls between them, written as a picture. A full stop is floor and every
-- other letter is a wall of some material, so that each room is built out of its own stuff and
-- you can tell where you are by the colour of the wall beside you.
--
--     w  the wallpaper of your own flat
--     b  the green panelling of the room that is also a bus
--     #  the stone of the corridor
--     d  the filing cabinets of the Department
--     L  the shelved spines of the library
--
-- Nothing here knows anything about drawing. It only knows what is where.


please define the building:
    remember rows is an empty list
    add "#wwwwwwww###################" to rows
    add "w........#.................#" to rows
    add "w........#.................#" to rows
    add "w..........................#" to rows
    add "w........#.................#" to rows
    add "w........#.................#" to rows
    add "#bbbb.bbb#.................#" to rows
    add "b........#.................#" to rows
    add "b........#.................#" to rows
    add "b..........................#" to rows
    add "b........#.................#" to rows
    add "b........#.................#" to rows
    add "#bbbbbbbb##.########.#######" to rows
    add "#dddddddddd.d#LLLLLL.LLLLLL#" to rows
    add "d............L.............L" to rows
    add "d............L.............L" to rows
    add "d..........................L" to rows
    add "d............L.............L" to rows
    add "d............L.............L" to rows
    add "d............L.............L" to rows
    add "#dddddddddddd#LLLLLLLLLLLLL#" to rows
    give back rows
thank you for defining


-- What stands at this square. Anywhere off the edge of the world counts as stone, so that a ray
-- cast out of the building still meets something and stops.
please define the stuff at with an ex and a why and a rows:
    check if ex is under 0:
        give back "#"
    thanks
    check if why is under 0:
        give back "#"
    thanks
    remember row is item the whole part of why plus 1 of rows or "#"
    give back the letter the whole part of ex plus 1 of row or "#"
thank you for defining


please define a wall at with an ex and a why and a rows:
    remember stuff is the stuff at with ex and why and rows
    give back stuff is not "."
thank you for defining


-- The three parts of the colour a material is painted in, before the light gets to it.
please define the paint of with a stuff:
    remember paint is an empty list
    check if stuff is "w":
        add 198 to paint
        add 174 to paint
        add 141 to paint
    otherwise if stuff is "b":
        add 74 to paint
        add 148 to paint
        add 118 to paint
    otherwise if stuff is "d":
        add 186 to paint
        add 176 to paint
        add 146 to paint
    otherwise if stuff is "L":
        add 158 to paint
        add 94 to paint
        add 74 to paint
    otherwise:
        add 132 to paint
        add 136 to paint
        add 146 to paint
    thank you for checking
    give back paint
thank you for defining


-- Which room a square belongs to, so that the screen can say where you are standing.
please define the room at with an ex and a why:
    check if why is under 12:
        check if ex is under 9:
            check if why is under 6:
                give back "Your Flat"
            thanks
            give back "The Room That Is Also A Bus"
        thanks
        give back "The Corridor"
    thanks
    check if ex is under 13:
        give back "The Department of Slightly Wrong Things"
    thanks
    give back "The Library"
thank you for defining


